IMPORT prelude

-- Vulnerable Adults Act 2018 (Singapore) -- who is a vulnerable adult (s 2), removal and its 14-working-day follow-up (ss 10,
-- 11), who may apply for which protection order (s 12), the advisers' panel (s 13(6)), committal periods and the residence
-- clean-up order (s 14(1), (2), (3)), the penalty for breaching a protection order (s 14(10)), expedited orders (s 15),
-- offence versus contempt (s 16), treatment without consent (s 18), the publication offence (s 22(6)) and protection for those
-- who give information (ss 9(4), 23(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/VAA2018.txt. The edition
-- states that it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; later amendments are annotated in the text,
-- the latest being Act 21 of 2023 (wef 2 January 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the decision points a family
-- member, caregiver, doctor, publisher or social worker would meet. Not encoded: the definitions of abuse, neglect and
-- self-neglect beyond their use as a single input; assessment powers (ss 5-7) except as context; entry, information and record
-- powers (ss 8, 9) except the immunity in s 9(4); designation of places (s 19); the Review Board (s 20); unlawful removal
-- (s 21); disclosure between agencies (s 24); enforcement powers, arrest and search (ss 26-29A); obstruction and false
-- information (ss 31, 32) beyond their penalties' shape; service (s 35); rules and regulations (ss 36, 37).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Vulnerable Adults Act 2018 -- protection`

§§ `2 -- vulnerable adult; working day`

-- s 2(1): "vulnerable adult" means an individual who "(a) is 18 years of age or older; and (b) is, by reason of mental or
-- physical infirmity, disability or incapacity, incapable of protecting himself or herself from abuse, neglect or self-neglect".
-- "working day" excludes any Sunday and public holiday. (Saturdays are therefore working days for this Act.)
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER, `incapable of self-protection by reason of infirmity, disability or incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is a vulnerable adult` IF
    `age in years` >= 18 AND `incapable of self-protection by reason of infirmity, disability or incapacity`

GIVEN `calendar days` IS A NUMBER, `Sundays among them` IS A NUMBER, `public holidays among them that are not Sundays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the working days` IS
    `calendar days` - `Sundays among them` - `public holidays among them that are not Sundays`

§§ `10 -- power to remove`

-- s 10(1): the Director-General or a protector may remove a vulnerable adult "if ... satisfied on reasonable grounds that the
-- vulnerable adult has experienced, or is experiencing or at risk of, abuse, neglect or self-neglect, and -- (a) the vulnerable
-- adult consents to the removal despite that another person is preventing the vulnerable adult's removal; (b) the vulnerable
-- adult is assessed by a mental capacity assessor to lack the mental capacity to consent; or (c) the vulnerable adult, where not
-- lacking mental capacity, does not consent to the removal, but is the subject of an order of court under subsection (4)."
-- s 10(2): where a donee or deputy is appointed, removal under (1)(b) needs no consent of the donee or deputy.
DECLARE `Removal stance` IS ONE OF
    `consents though another person is preventing removal`
    `assessed to lack capacity to consent`
    `has capacity and refuses`

GIVEN `reasonable grounds of abuse, neglect or self-neglect` IS A BOOLEAN, `the adult's stance` IS A `Removal stance`, `a section 10(4) court order exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `removal is authorised` IF
    `reasonable grounds of abuse, neglect or self-neglect`
    AND CONSIDER `the adult's stance`
        WHEN `consents though another person is preventing removal` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `assessed to lack capacity to consent` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `has capacity and refuses` THEN `a section 10(4) court order exists`

§§ `11 -- after removal`

-- s 11(1): after removal the Director-General or protector must "(a) commit the vulnerable adult to a place of temporary care
-- and protection or to the care of a fit person; and (b) within 14 working days after the day of the removal, apply to a court
-- under section 12 ... or apply for an order under subsection (2), unless [they] earlier permit the vulnerable adult" to return.
-- s 11(2): if a s 12 application cannot be made in time, they must within that time apply for custody, charge and care meanwhile.
GIVEN `working days since removal` IS A NUMBER, `an application under section 12 or 11(2) was made` IS A BOOLEAN, `the adult was earlier permitted to return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 14-working-day duty is breached` IF
    `working days since removal` > 14
    AND (NOT `an application under section 12 or 11(2) was made`)
    AND (NOT `the adult was earlier permitted to return`)

§§ `12 -- who may apply for which order`

-- s 14(1) orders: (a) committal up to 6 months; (b) committal over 6 months; (c) production for treatment; (d) supervision;
-- (e) restraining an abuser; (f) exclusive occupation; (g) staying away from an area; (h) no visiting or communicating;
-- (i) counselling; (j) making the residence safe. s 15: expedited order.
DECLARE `Order` IS ONE OF
    `committal up to 6 months`
    `committal beyond 6 months`
    `production for treatment`
    `supervision`
    `restraining the abuser`
    `exclusive occupation`
    `area exclusion`
    `no visiting or communicating`
    `counselling`
    `making the residence safe`
    `an expedited order`

DECLARE `Applicant` IS ONE OF
    `the Director-General or a protector`
    `an approved welfare officer`
    `the adult's donee or deputy`
    `a family member`
    `the vulnerable adult`

-- "section 14(1)(e), (f), (g) or (h) or 15": the orders that persons other than the Director-General or a protector may seek.
GIVEN `the order` IS AN `Order`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is a personal protection order` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `restraining the abuser` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `exclusive occupation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `area exclusion` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `no visiting or communicating` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an expedited order` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 12(2)(a), where the adult "is assessed by a mental capacity assessor to lack the mental capacity to consent to the
-- application": the Director-General or a protector, any order; an approved welfare officer or the donee or deputy, or a family
-- member, the personal protection orders. (b) "in any other case": the Director-General or a protector, any order; an approved
-- welfare officer "with the consent of the vulnerable adult"; "the vulnerable adult may, on his or her own"; a family member
-- "with the consent of the vulnerable adult" -- the latter three only for the personal protection orders. The donee or deputy is
-- not listed in (b); the vulnerable adult is not listed in (a).
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant`, `the order` IS AN `Order`, `the adult is assessed to lack capacity to consent to the application` IS A BOOLEAN, `the adult consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant may apply` IF
    CONSIDER `the applicant`
    WHEN `the Director-General or a protector` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an approved welfare officer` THEN
        `the order is a personal protection order` `the order`
        AND (`the adult is assessed to lack capacity to consent to the application` OR `the adult consents`)
    WHEN `the adult's donee or deputy` THEN
        `the order is a personal protection order` `the order`
        AND `the adult is assessed to lack capacity to consent to the application`
    WHEN `a family member` THEN
        `the order is a personal protection order` `the order`
        AND (`the adult is assessed to lack capacity to consent to the application` OR `the adult consents`)
    WHEN `the vulnerable adult` THEN
        `the order is a personal protection order` `the order`
        AND (NOT `the adult is assessed to lack capacity to consent to the application`)

§§ `13(6) -- advisers`

-- s 13(6): "A judge of the court, when determining whether to make an order under section 14(1)(b) or (j), must sit with 2
-- advisers from a panel of advisers nominated by the Minister." (7): unless the court cannot be fully constituted without an
-- adjournment that would be inexpedient, when the judge may sit with one adviser or alone.
GIVEN `the order` IS AN `Order`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the judge must sit with 2 advisers` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `committal beyond 6 months` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `making the residence safe` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `14(1)(a), (b) -- committal periods`

-- s 14(1)(a): committal to a place of temporary care and protection or a fit person "for a period not exceeding 6 months";
-- (b): to a place of safety or a fit person "for a specified period exceeding 6 months where the court is satisfied that it is
-- in the best interests of the vulnerable adult to be so committed".
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER, `the court is satisfied it is in the adult's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a committal of that length is available` IF
    `months` <= 6 OR `the court is satisfied it is in the adult's best interests`

§§ `14(2), (3) -- making the residence safe`

-- s 14(2): subject to (3), an order under (1)(j) only "(a) with the consent of every owner of the residence and of the
-- vulnerable adult; or (b) where the owner or owners ... cannot be located after reasonable attempts ... (i) with the consent of
-- the vulnerable adult; and (ii) after a notice by advertisement ... and the prescribed period after such publication has lapsed
-- without any owner objecting".
-- s 14(3): without the adult's consent only "(i) if the vulnerable adult lacks the mental capacity to consent; or (ii) if the
-- court is of the view that such an order is necessary for the protection and safety of the vulnerable adult"; without an
-- owner's consent only "(i) if the owner lacks the mental capacity to consent; or (ii)" the same necessity.
-- Reading: (3) is the route around the consents in (2). The unlocated-owner route in (2)(b) is read as standing in for owner
-- consent. That is an inference about how (2) and (3) combine; the text says only "subject to subsection (3)".
GIVEN `the adult consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `the adult lacks capacity to consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `every owner consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `owners unlocated, advertised, period lapsed with no objection` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner lacks capacity to consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court finds the order necessary for protection and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a residence order may be made` IF
        (`the adult consents` OR `the adult lacks capacity to consent` OR `the court finds the order necessary for protection and safety`)
    AND (`every owner consents` OR `owners unlocated, advertised, period lapsed with no objection` OR `the owner lacks capacity to consent` OR `the court finds the order necessary for protection and safety`)

§§ `14(10), 15(8), 22(6) -- penalties`

-- s 14(10): failing without reasonable excuse to comply with an order under (1)(e), (f), (g) or (h): "(a) on the first
-- conviction ... a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or both; and (b) on a second
-- or subsequent conviction ... a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 18 months or both"
-- [Act 21 of 2023 wef 02/01/2025]. s 15(8): breach of an expedited order, $5,000 or 12 months.
GIVEN `prior convictions under 14(10)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months for breaching a protection order` IS
    IF `prior convictions under 14(10)` >= 1 THEN 18 ELSE 12

-- s 22(6): publication identifying a vulnerable adult without the Director-General's approval: "a fine not exceeding $5,000
-- and, in the case of a second or subsequent conviction, to a fine not exceeding $10,000". No imprisonment is provided.
GIVEN `prior convictions under 22(6)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine for an identifying publication` IS
    IF `prior convictions under 22(6)` >= 1 THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

§§ `15 -- expedited order`

-- s 15(3): an expedited order takes effect "from the date on which the order is served on that person" (or a later date the
-- court specifies). (4): it "ceases to have effect on the earlier of ... (a) the date that is 28 days after the date the order
-- is made; (b) the date the court decides the application under section 12." (5): "Despite subsection (4), the court may extend
-- the duration".
-- Reading: an extension is taken to displace both limbs of (4). That is an inference; (5) does not say which limb it reaches.
GIVEN `served on the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since the order was made` IS A NUMBER, `the section 12 application is decided` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court extended it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the expedited order is in force` IF
    `served on the respondent`
    AND (`the court extended it`
         OR (`days since the order was made` < 28 AND (NOT `the section 12 application is decided`)))

§§ `16 -- offence or contempt, not both`

-- s 16(2): where a person is convicted under s 14(10), (13)(a) or 15(8) for a non-compliance, "that non-compliance is not
-- punishable as a contempt of court". (3): a person cannot be convicted for a non-compliance "which has been punished as a
-- contempt of court".
GIVEN `already convicted of the offence for it` IS A BOOLEAN, `already punished as a contempt for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-compliance can be punished as a contempt` IF
    NOT `already convicted of the offence for it`

GIVEN `already convicted of the offence for it` IS A BOOLEAN, `already punished as a contempt for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-compliance can found a conviction` IF
    NOT `already punished as a contempt for it`

§§ `18 -- treatment without consent`

-- s 18(2): treatment "may be administered ... only with the vulnerable adult's consent unless -- (a) the vulnerable adult is
-- assessed by a mental capacity assessor to lack the mental capacity to consent, and the registered medical practitioner or
-- registered dentist reasonably believes that it is in the vulnerable adult's best interests ...; or (b) it is not practicable to
-- obtain consent ..., and the [practitioner] (i) reasonably believes that a medical or dental emergency ... exists; and (ii) is of
-- the view that it is in the vulnerable adult's best interests".
GIVEN `the adult consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `assessed to lack capacity to consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent is impracticable to obtain` IS A BOOLEAN, `the practitioner believes there is an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN, `the practitioner believes it is in the adult's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `treatment may be administered` IF
        `the adult consents`
    OR  (`assessed to lack capacity to consent` AND `the practitioner believes it is in the adult's best interests`)
    OR  (`consent is impracticable to obtain` AND `the practitioner believes there is an emergency` AND `the practitioner believes it is in the adult's best interests`)

§§ `9(4), 23(2) -- protection for those who give information`

-- s 23(1): any person who knows or has reason to suspect abuse, neglect or self-neglect "may notify" the Director-General, a
-- protector or an authorised person. (2)(b): the notifier, "insofar as the person has acted with reasonable care and in good
-- faith, incurs no civil or criminal liability". s 9(4)(b): a person who gives information or record access as DIRECTED under s 9
-- "to the extent the person has acted in good faith, incurs no civil or criminal liability" -- good faith alone.
DECLARE `Disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `a voluntary notification under section 23`
    `information given as directed under section 9`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A `Disclosure`, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discloser is free of civil and criminal liability` IF
    CONSIDER `the disclosure`
    WHEN `a voluntary notification under section 23` THEN `acted in good faith` AND `acted with reasonable care`
    WHEN `information given as directed under section 9` THEN `acted in good faith`
